<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Septem</h1><p class="st-meta">534 CE – 711 CE (approx.) · capital Septem</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Byzantine fortress of Ceuta on the Strait of Gibraltar, the last outpost of Roman rule in north-west Africa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After Justinian's conquest of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vandal-kingdom">Vandal Kingdom</a> in 534, Byzantine forces occupied Septem (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a>), named after its seven hills, at the African side of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-gibraltar">Strait of Gibraltar</a>. Justinian had its walls rebuilt and a church to the Virgin built there, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a> records.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Septem was a small garrison town, commanded by a tribune and supported by a fleet watching the Strait and Visigothic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. It belonged to the province of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-mauretania">Mauretania</a> Secunda and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/exarchate-of-africa">Exarchate of Africa</a>. Little is known of its internal life, though it remained Christian and Latin-speaking amid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> territory.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Arab conquest of the rest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, Septem stood isolated. Tradition says its governor, Count Julian, aided the Arab invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and the town passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> around 711. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> later became Portuguese and then Spanish.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 534 CE – 711 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p